// Project message types for the {{project_name}} guest: user-defined
// procedure types declared in WIT, consumed two ways from the same file:
//
//   - `mgen message -i wit/types.wit -o gentypes/Types.h -l c` generates
//     the C structs plus their xxx_encode/xxx_decode codecs as a
//     self-contained header — see the Makefile `gentypes` task;
//   - `mtp ... --type-wit wit/types.wit` registers these names so procedure
//     annotations in src/procedures.c may use them (record
//     parameters/returns, enum parameters) — see the Makefile `transpile`
//     task.
//
// On the procedure byte pipe a record travels as the positional
// `uni-data-value` record case (declaration order, names dropped by the
// host); the desc JSON keys are the WIT field names verbatim.
//
// The `package` clause matches the mtp-generated world.wit: one WIT
// directory is one package, and the `wasm-tools component embed` world
// build rejects headerless files sitting next to a packaged world. The
// world does not reference this interface; it rides along inertly.
package mududb:{{kebab_name}};

interface types {
    // The item fact sheet: scalar fields (u32 and bool both cross the host
    // as i32 — bool as 0/1) and a list field.
    record item-info {
        name: string,
        price: u32,
        in-stock: bool,
        labels: list<string>,
    }
}
